extends /specs/products/pericles/page-structure/structure/templates/structure/layout-tmpl.jade
block content


    section.source_section
        h2 List variations

        h3 Ordered list
        .source_example
            ol
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie

        h3 Ordered alpha list
        .source_example
            ol.upper-alpha
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie


        h3 Unstyled list
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used the default class `rlist`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie

        h3 Inline list
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used `rlist--inline`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist--inline
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie

        h3 Inline seperated list
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used `rlist--inline` and `separator`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist--inline.separator
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie

        h3 List with separator - bottom
        markdown
            p adding `separator` class to `rlist` list will add separator between items "to the bottom of each item".
        .source_example
            ul.rlist.separator
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie


        h3 Unordered list with blue bullets
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used the default class `unordered-list`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist.unordered-list
                li Nick Gayeski
                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie

        h3 Unordered bordered list with blue bullets
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used the default class `unordered-bordered-list`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist.unordered-bordered-list
                li
                    a Nick Gayeski
                li
                    a George Pess
                li
                    a Tim Beechie


        h3 Unordered bordered list with blue bullets
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used the default class `unordered-list-icons`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist.unordered-list-icons
                li
                    a
                        i(aria-hidden='true' class='icon-notice')
                        | Submit an article
                li
                    a
                        i(aria-hidden='true' class='icon-notice')
                        | Browse free sample issue
                li
                    a
                        i(aria-hidden='true' class='icon-notice')
                        | Get content alerts
                li
                    a
                        i(aria-hidden='true' class='icon-notice')
                        | Subscribe to this journal
                Li
                    a
                        i(aria-hidden='true' class='icon-notice')
                        | Recommend to a librarian

        h3 Unordered list with border on the left used on home page
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used the default class `list--bordered-left`.
        .source_example
            ul.rlist.list--bordered-left
                li
                    a(href="#")
                        | Submit an article
                li
                    a
                        | Browse free sample issue
                li
                    a
                        | Get content alerts
                li
                    a
                        | Subscribe to this journal
                Li
                    a
                        | Recommend to a librarian
        h3 expandable-list
        markdown
            p In the example below we've used `separated-list` class to add a borders above and below the list
        .source_example
            ul.rlist
                li
                    div.expandable-list
                        a.expandable-list__toggle(href='#' data-toggle='dropdown' id="pane-1")
                            i.icon-add_box(aria-hidden="true")
                            | list
                        ul.rlist.expandable-list__body( aria-hidden='true' aria-labelledby="pane-1")
                            li reem
                            li majid
                            li ali

                li George Pess
                li Tim Beechie

    | #{''}